Subject: [PATCH] fix: preserve MCP tool policy across alias changes

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: keep MCP tool allowlists and denylists effective across
aliases, reconnects, and server lifecycle changes
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1008-personal-feature-add-worker-blueprints-with-runtime-integration.patch, 1011-personal-feature-add-hook-context-and-post-tool-transform.patch, 1012-personal-feature-add-delegation-efficiency-measurement.patch

Patch intent:
Preserve MCP tool-policy identity across generated aliases, reconnects, and
server lifecycle changes so session allowlists and denylists remain effective.

Why it exists:
MCP tool aliases can change when servers refresh or reconnect. Policy must
follow the stable server and raw tool identity rather than only one alias.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/mod.rs owns the Registry MCP surface,
MCP dispatch policy checks, tool refresh, reconciliation, and unregistration.

Update guidance:
Preserve current and historical alias tracking, check all identities against
session policy, and rebuild the index whenever the MCP tool surface changes.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core mcp_collision_refresh_preserves_offline_cache_and_legacy_allowlists --lib
